          "en": "Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. © Thales Group Page 175 of 819 KEKGEN – 6.3 Variant LMK  Key Block LMK  Available in package(s): Premium Authorization: Not required Function: To generate a KEK send key and KEK receive key, return the keys enciphered under a KTK (ZMK) with appropriate variants and under the LMK. Notes: If no key scheme flags are supplied, the HSM will use the single length KTK (ZMK) ariant on the output KEKs & KEKr. If key scheme flags are supplied the HSM uses the appropriate variant of ZMK, depending on length for the output KEKs & KEKr."
