    "source": "Thales payShield 10K Host Command Reference v2.3, Section 2.1, Command GA (p. 270)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command GA (GB) - Derive a PIN Using the Diebold Method\n\n- **Command Code:** `GA`\n- **Response Code(s):** `GB`\n- **Manual Page:** 270\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v2.3\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nDerive a PIN using the Diebold method.\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `GA` |\n| Index Flag | 1 A | Value ' K ' . |\n| Table Pointer | 3 H | The value of the base location of the Diebold table. |\n| Algorithm Number | 2 H | The number of the Diebold algorithm required. |\n| Offset | 4 N | For a derived PIN, this is ' 0000 ' . Otherwise, an offset can be used. Primary Account Number (PAN) 12 N If a 3DES Key Block or Variant LMK is used: The 12 right - most digits of the PAN ( excluding the check digit) . or n N If an AES Key Block LMK is used: The full 12 - 19 digit PAN (including the check digit). If present, the delimiter below must also be present. |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ';'. Only present if an AES Key Block LMK is used. |\n| PIN Validation Data | 16 A | User - defined data consisting of hexadecimal characters and the character ' N ' , which indicates to the HSM where to insert the last 5 digits of the PAN . The data must be right - justified and padded with ' F ' s. |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `GB` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command GA (GB) - Derive a PIN Using the Diebold Method\n\n- **Command Code:** `GA`\n- **Response Code(s):** `GB`\n- **Manual Page:** 270\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v2.3\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nDerive a PIN using the Diebold method.\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `GA` |\n| Index Flag | 1 A | Value ' K ' . |\n| Table Pointer | 3 H | The value of the base location of the Diebold table. |\n| Algorithm Number | 2 H | The number of the Diebold algorithm required. |\n| Offset | 4 N | For a derived PIN, this is ' 0000 ' . Otherwise, an offset can be used. Primary Account Number (PAN) 12 N If a 3DES Key Block or Variant LMK is used: The 12 right - most digits of the PAN ( excluding the check digit) . or n N If an AES Key Block LMK is used: The full 12 - 19 digit PAN (including the check digit). If present, the delimiter below must also be present. |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ';'. Only present if an AES Key Block LMK is used. |\n| PIN Validation Data | 16 A | User - defined data consisting of hexadecimal characters and the character ' N ' , which indicates to the HSM where to insert the last 5 digits of the PAN . The data must be right - justified and padded with ' F ' s. |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `GB` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n"
    }
