    "source": "Thales payShield 10K Host Command Reference v2.3, Section 2.1, Command K2 (p. 557)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command K2 (K3) - Verify Truncated Application Cryptogram ( Mastercard CAP)\n\n- **Command Code:** `K2`\n- **Response Code(s):** `K3`\n- **Manual Page:** 557\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v2.3\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nValidate a Truncated Application Cryptogram (Mastercard CAP).\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `K2` |\n| Mode Flag | 1 H | Mode of operation: ' 0 ' : Perform Truncated AC verification and MAC verification. |\n| Scheme ID | 2 N | ' 00 ' : Mastercard CAP ' 01 ' : Mastercard CAP with TDS. ICC Master Key Derivation Method 1 N Identifies the DK - AC key derivation method: ' 0 ' : EMV 4.1 Master Key Derivation Option A ' 1 ' : EMV 4.1 Master Key Derivation Option B Session Key Derivation Method 1 N ' 0 ' : No Session Key SK - AC used for Application Cryptograms ' 1 ' : Mastercard (M/Chip 2.1 method) ' 2 ' : EMV 4.1 (EMV2000) method ' 3 ' : EMV 4.1 (EMV Common Session Key Derivation Method) MK - AC (under LMK) The Issuer Master Key for generating and verifying Application Cryptograms. 32 H or ' U ' + 32 H For a Variant LM K , the ' MK - AC ' must be encrypted under LMK pair 28 - 29 variant 1. or ' S ' + n A For a Key Block LMK, the ' MK - AC ' must comply with the following: Key Usage Algorithm Mode of Use ' E0 ' ' T ' 'X', 'N' |\n| IV - AC | 16 B | Only present for Session Key Derivation Method = ' 2 ' . IV for EMV2000 Application Cryptogram session key derivation |\n| PAN Length | 2 N | Only present for ICC Master Key Derivation Method = ' 1 ' . Length in bytes of PAN/PAN Sequence Number field. Valid values ' 01 ' ... ' 99 ' . Note: This field indicates the number of bytes used to store the PAN/PSN. If the number of digits in the PAN/PSN is odd, an extra ' 0 ' digit must be inserted to the left. |\n| PAN/PAN Sequence No | 8 B |  or n B For ICC Master Key Derivation Method = ' 0 ' , this field will be fixed at 8 bytes, and will contain the pre - formatted PAN/PSN (in BCD format). Note: It is the responsibility of the host system to ensure that the PAN/PSN is |\n| appropriately padded to | 8 b | ytes, according to EMV Option A. For ICC Master Key Derivation Method = ' 1 ' , this field contains the PAN/PSN (in BCD format). The field length is specified (in bytes) by the \" PAN Length \" field. Note: It is the responsibility of the host system to ensure that the PAN/PSN is an even number of digits (therefore a whole number of bytes) by pre - pending an extra ' 0 ' digit to the left if necessary. The PAN/PSN is then used as in EMV Option B. |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `K3` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command K2 (K3) - Verify Truncated Application Cryptogram ( Mastercard CAP)\n\n- **Command Code:** `K2`\n- **Response Code(s):** `K3`\n- **Manual Page:** 557\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v2.3\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nValidate a Truncated Application Cryptogram (Mastercard CAP).\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `K2` |\n| Mode Flag | 1 H | Mode of operation: ' 0 ' : Perform Truncated AC verification and MAC verification. |\n| Scheme ID | 2 N | ' 00 ' : Mastercard CAP ' 01 ' : Mastercard CAP with TDS. ICC Master Key Derivation Method 1 N Identifies the DK - AC key derivation method: ' 0 ' : EMV 4.1 Master Key Derivation Option A ' 1 ' : EMV 4.1 Master Key Derivation Option B Session Key Derivation Method 1 N ' 0 ' : No Session Key SK - AC used for Application Cryptograms ' 1 ' : Mastercard (M/Chip 2.1 method) ' 2 ' : EMV 4.1 (EMV2000) method ' 3 ' : EMV 4.1 (EMV Common Session Key Derivation Method) MK - AC (under LMK) The Issuer Master Key for generating and verifying Application Cryptograms. 32 H or ' U ' + 32 H For a Variant LM K , the ' MK - AC ' must be encrypted under LMK pair 28 - 29 variant 1. or ' S ' + n A For a Key Block LMK, the ' MK - AC ' must comply with the following: Key Usage Algorithm Mode of Use ' E0 ' ' T ' 'X', 'N' |\n| IV - AC | 16 B | Only present for Session Key Derivation Method = ' 2 ' . IV for EMV2000 Application Cryptogram session key derivation |\n| PAN Length | 2 N | Only present for ICC Master Key Derivation Method = ' 1 ' . Length in bytes of PAN/PAN Sequence Number field. Valid values ' 01 ' ... ' 99 ' . Note: This field indicates the number of bytes used to store the PAN/PSN. If the number of digits in the PAN/PSN is odd, an extra ' 0 ' digit must be inserted to the left. |\n| PAN/PAN Sequence No | 8 B |  or n B For ICC Master Key Derivation Method = ' 0 ' , this field will be fixed at 8 bytes, and will contain the pre - formatted PAN/PSN (in BCD format). Note: It is the responsibility of the host system to ensure that the PAN/PSN is |\n| appropriately padded to | 8 b | ytes, according to EMV Option A. For ICC Master Key Derivation Method = ' 1 ' , this field contains the PAN/PSN (in BCD format). The field length is specified (in bytes) by the \" PAN Length \" field. Note: It is the responsibility of the host system to ensure that the PAN/PSN is an even number of digits (therefore a whole number of bytes) by pre - pending an extra ' 0 ' digit to the left if necessary. The PAN/PSN is then used as in EMV Option B. |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `K3` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n"
    }
