    "source": "Thales payShield 10K Host Command Reference v2.3, Section 2.1, Command KO (p. 576)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command KO (KP) - Generate Card RSA Key Set and Public Key Certificate\n\n- **Command Code:** `KO`\n- **Response Code(s):** `KP`\n- **Manual Page:** 576\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v2.3\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nGenerate a Card RSA Key Set and create the requested Certificate for the Public Key signed by the Issuer ' s Private Key.\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `KO` |\n| Scheme ID | 1 N | ' 0 ' : Visa VSDC ' 1 ' : Mastercard ' 2 ' : American Express AEIPS V4.1 ' 3 ' : JCB ' 4 ' : Union Pay ' 5 ' : Discover The Scheme ID parameter is not used in the processing at this time. It is included for any future differentiations in the Schemes. |\n| Certificate Type | 1 N | ' 0 ' : Card Public Key Certificate ' 1 ' : Card PIN Encipherment Public Key Certificate |\n| Mode Flag | 1 N | ' 0 ' : Generate RSA Key Set and Certificate, using Strong Primes ' 1 ' : Generate Certificate with provided Public Key and export the provided Private Key under the KEK in the requested format ' 2 ' : Generate RSA Key Set and Certificate, using Standard Primes |\n| RSA Key Mode Flag | 1 N | Indicates the type of keys required ' 0 ' : Keys with q > p ' 2 ' : Keys with p > q Note: For provided key sets, the command will verify the type of key provided and modify the key parameters to comply with this condition. If Mode Flag = ' 0 ' or ' 2 ' , the following field must be present: |\n| Key Length | 4 N | Modulus length in bits (must be a multiple of 8) minimum value = ' 0400 ' , maximum value = ' 2040 ' . The following fields must be present as noted below: Card Private Key Output format 2 N Output format for Card Private Key: ' 03 ' : Output in the form of 5 Chinese Remainder Theorem components CBC encrypted (with IV = 0x0000000000000000) under the K EK. See Card Issuing Appendix H – Private Key Encodings |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `KP` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command KO (KP) - Generate Card RSA Key Set and Public Key Certificate\n\n- **Command Code:** `KO`\n- **Response Code(s):** `KP`\n- **Manual Page:** 576\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v2.3\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nGenerate a Card RSA Key Set and create the requested Certificate for the Public Key signed by the Issuer ' s Private Key.\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `KO` |\n| Scheme ID | 1 N | ' 0 ' : Visa VSDC ' 1 ' : Mastercard ' 2 ' : American Express AEIPS V4.1 ' 3 ' : JCB ' 4 ' : Union Pay ' 5 ' : Discover The Scheme ID parameter is not used in the processing at this time. It is included for any future differentiations in the Schemes. |\n| Certificate Type | 1 N | ' 0 ' : Card Public Key Certificate ' 1 ' : Card PIN Encipherment Public Key Certificate |\n| Mode Flag | 1 N | ' 0 ' : Generate RSA Key Set and Certificate, using Strong Primes ' 1 ' : Generate Certificate with provided Public Key and export the provided Private Key under the KEK in the requested format ' 2 ' : Generate RSA Key Set and Certificate, using Standard Primes |\n| RSA Key Mode Flag | 1 N | Indicates the type of keys required ' 0 ' : Keys with q > p ' 2 ' : Keys with p > q Note: For provided key sets, the command will verify the type of key provided and modify the key parameters to comply with this condition. If Mode Flag = ' 0 ' or ' 2 ' , the following field must be present: |\n| Key Length | 4 N | Modulus length in bits (must be a multiple of 8) minimum value = ' 0400 ' , maximum value = ' 2040 ' . The following fields must be present as noted below: Card Private Key Output format 2 N Output format for Card Private Key: ' 03 ' : Output in the form of 5 Chinese Remainder Theorem components CBC encrypted (with IV = 0x0000000000000000) under the K EK. See Card Issuing Appendix H – Private Key Encodings |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `KP` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n"
    }
