    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command CA (CB) - Translate a PIN from TPK to ZPK/BDK Encryption ( 3DES DUKPT)\n\n- **Command Code:** `CA`\n- **Response Code(s):** `CB`\n- **Manual Page:** 334\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTranslate a PIN from encryption under a TPK to encryption under an interchange key (ZPK) or a DUKPT key for transmission to another node. If the same PIN block format is defined, only the key is translated. Note that translation to BDK encryption is only permitted if the security setting \" Enable PIN translation to BDK encryption \" is \"YES\".\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `CA` |\n| Destination Key Flag | 1 A | For a Variant LMK only. Value ' * ' (X ' 2A). Optional; if present, this flag indicates that the destination key is a BDK - 1. Value ' ~ ' (X ' 7E). Optional; if present, this flag indicates that the destination key is a BDK - 2. Destination Key The key under which the PIN block is to be encrypted. Three types of keys are supported: ZPK, BDK - 1 and BDK - 2. 16/32 H or ' U ' + 32 H or ' T ' + 48 H For a Variant LMK: If ' Destination Key Flag ' is not present, then this key must be a ZPK, encrypted under LMK 06 - 07. If ' Destination Key Flag ' is ' * ' , then this key must be a BDK - 1, encrypted under LMK 28 - 29. If ' Destination Key Flag ' is ' ~ ' , then this key must be a BDK - 2, encrypted under LMK 28 - 29/6. or ' S ' + n A For a Key Block LMK: This key must be either a ZPK or BDK - 1 or BDK - 2, and comply with the following: |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `CB` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command CA (CB) - Translate a PIN from TPK to ZPK/BDK Encryption ( 3DES DUKPT)\n\n- **Command Code:** `CA`\n- **Response Code(s):** `CB`\n- **Manual Page:** 334\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTranslate a PIN from encryption under a TPK to encryption under an interchange key (ZPK) or a DUKPT key for transmission to another node. If the same PIN block format is defined, only the key is translated. Note that translation to BDK encryption is only permitted if the security setting \" Enable PIN translation to BDK encryption \" is \"YES\".\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `CA` |\n| Destination Key Flag | 1 A | For a Variant LMK only. Value ' * ' (X ' 2A). Optional; if present, this flag indicates that the destination key is a BDK - 1. Value ' ~ ' (X ' 7E). Optional; if present, this flag indicates that the destination key is a BDK - 2. Destination Key The key under which the PIN block is to be encrypted. Three types of keys are supported: ZPK, BDK - 1 and BDK - 2. 16/32 H or ' U ' + 32 H or ' T ' + 48 H For a Variant LMK: If ' Destination Key Flag ' is not present, then this key must be a ZPK, encrypted under LMK 06 - 07. If ' Destination Key Flag ' is ' * ' , then this key must be a BDK - 1, encrypted under LMK 28 - 29. If ' Destination Key Flag ' is ' ~ ' , then this key must be a BDK - 2, encrypted under LMK 28 - 29/6. or ' S ' + n A For a Key Block LMK: This key must be either a ZPK or BDK - 1 or BDK - 2, and comply with the following: |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `CB` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n"
    }
