    "source": "Thales payShield 10K Host Command Reference v1.9, Section 2.1, Command D0 (p. 668)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command D0 (D1) - Generate a PIN Pad Authentication Code\n\n- **Command Code:** `D0`\n- **Response Code(s):** `D1`\n- **Manual Page:** 668\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTo generate a PIN Pad Authentication Code (PPAC).\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `D0` |\n| KMA | 16 H |  or |\n| 1 A + | 32 H |  or |\n| 1 A + | 48 H |  KMA, encrypted under LMK pair 14 - 15 variant 0 if the security setting \" Enforce key type 002 separation for PCI HSM compliance \" has the value \" N \" , or under LMK pair 36 - 37 variant 8 if the setting has the value \" Y \" . |\n| PPSN | 16 N | PIN Pad Serial Number |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Must be present if a message trailer is present. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Optional. Maximum length 32 characters . |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `D1` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n| PPAC | 8 H | PIN Pad Authentication Code |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Present only if present in the command message. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. © Thales Group Page 669 of 806 Encrypt a CPAT Authentication Value Variant LMK  Key Block LMK  Available in package(s): Premium Authorization: Not required Function: To encrypt a CPAT Authentication Value (CAV). Notes: The CAV is encrypted with a privacy key, denoted KD, which is derived from the current value of the Transaction Key (KT), the Systems Trace Audit Number (STAN) and the Card Acceptor Terminal Identification (CATID) according to the method defined in AS2805 Appendix N – B: Derivation of Data Values for 16H and AS2805 Appendix N – E: Privacy Key Derivation for 32H key lengths. |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value ' D8 ' |\n| KT | 16 H |  or |\n| 1 A + | 32 H |  KT, encrypted under LMK pair 14 - 15 variant 0 if the security setting \" Enforce key type 002 separation for PCI HSM compliance \" has the value \" N \" , or under LMK pair 36 - 37 variant 8 if the setting has the value \" Y \" . |\n| STAN | 6 N | Systems Trace Audit Number |\n| CATID | 16 H | Card Acceptor Terminal Identification |\n| CAV | 16 H | CPAT Authentication Value |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Must be present if a message trailer is present. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Optional. Maximum length 32 characters . RESPONSE MESSAGE ' 10 ' : KT parity error ' 12 ' : No keys loaded in user storage ' 13 ' : LMK error; report to supervisor ' 15 ' : Error in input data ' 21 ' : Invalid user storage index |\n| Encrypted CAV | 16 H | CAV, encrypted with KD |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Present only if present in the command message. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command D0 (D1) - Generate a PIN Pad Authentication Code\n\n- **Command Code:** `D0`\n- **Response Code(s):** `D1`\n- **Manual Page:** 668\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTo generate a PIN Pad Authentication Code (PPAC).\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `D0` |\n| KMA | 16 H |  or |\n| 1 A + | 32 H |  or |\n| 1 A + | 48 H |  KMA, encrypted under LMK pair 14 - 15 variant 0 if the security setting \" Enforce key type 002 separation for PCI HSM compliance \" has the value \" N \" , or under LMK pair 36 - 37 variant 8 if the setting has the value \" Y \" . |\n| PPSN | 16 N | PIN Pad Serial Number |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Must be present if a message trailer is present. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Optional. Maximum length 32 characters . |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `D1` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n| PPAC | 8 H | PIN Pad Authentication Code |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Present only if present in the command message. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. © Thales Group Page 669 of 806 Encrypt a CPAT Authentication Value Variant LMK  Key Block LMK  Available in package(s): Premium Authorization: Not required Function: To encrypt a CPAT Authentication Value (CAV). Notes: The CAV is encrypted with a privacy key, denoted KD, which is derived from the current value of the Transaction Key (KT), the Systems Trace Audit Number (STAN) and the Card Acceptor Terminal Identification (CATID) according to the method defined in AS2805 Appendix N – B: Derivation of Data Values for 16H and AS2805 Appendix N – E: Privacy Key Derivation for 32H key lengths. |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value ' D8 ' |\n| KT | 16 H |  or |\n| 1 A + | 32 H |  KT, encrypted under LMK pair 14 - 15 variant 0 if the security setting \" Enforce key type 002 separation for PCI HSM compliance \" has the value \" N \" , or under LMK pair 36 - 37 variant 8 if the setting has the value \" Y \" . |\n| STAN | 6 N | Systems Trace Audit Number |\n| CATID | 16 H | Card Acceptor Terminal Identification |\n| CAV | 16 H | CPAT Authentication Value |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Must be present if a message trailer is present. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Optional. Maximum length 32 characters . RESPONSE MESSAGE ' 10 ' : KT parity error ' 12 ' : No keys loaded in user storage ' 13 ' : LMK error; report to supervisor ' 15 ' : Error in input data ' 21 ' : Invalid user storage index |\n| Encrypted CAV | 16 H | CAV, encrypted with KD |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Present only if present in the command message. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. |\n\n"
    }
