    "source": "Thales payShield 10K Host Command Reference v1.9, Section 2.1, Command EM (p. 196)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command EM (EN) - Translate a Private Key\n\n- **Command Code:** `EM`\n- **Response Code(s):** `EN`\n- **Manual Page:** 196\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTranslate an RSA or ECC private key from encryption under an ' old ' LMK to encryption under the ' new ' LMK. The ' old ' or ' new ' LMK must have previously been loaded into Key Change\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `EM` |\n| Private key length | 4 N | For a Variant LMK: Length (in bytes) of the next field. or 4 H For a Key Block LMK: This field is ignored, and should be set to ' FFFF ' . Private key The Private Key to be translated. n B For a Variant LM K , the ' Private Key ' must be encrypted under LMK pair 34 - 35. or ' S ' + n B For a Key Block LMK, the ' Private Key ' must comply with the following: Key Usage Algorithm Mode of Use ' 03 ' , ' 04 ' , ' 05 ' , ' 06 ' ' R ' ' S ' , ' D ' , ' N ' '03' 'E' 'S', 'X', 'N' |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `EN` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command EM (EN) - Translate a Private Key\n\n- **Command Code:** `EM`\n- **Response Code(s):** `EN`\n- **Manual Page:** 196\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTranslate an RSA or ECC private key from encryption under an ' old ' LMK to encryption under the ' new ' LMK. The ' old ' or ' new ' LMK must have previously been loaded into Key Change\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `EM` |\n| Private key length | 4 N | For a Variant LMK: Length (in bytes) of the next field. or 4 H For a Key Block LMK: This field is ignored, and should be set to ' FFFF ' . Private key The Private Key to be translated. n B For a Variant LM K , the ' Private Key ' must be encrypted under LMK pair 34 - 35. or ' S ' + n B For a Key Block LMK, the ' Private Key ' must comply with the following: Key Usage Algorithm Mode of Use ' 03 ' , ' 04 ' , ' 05 ' , ' 06 ' ' R ' ' S ' , ' D ' , ' N ' '03' 'E' 'S', 'X', 'N' |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `EN` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n\n"
    }
