          "en": "Restricted to the following: ' 01 ' : ISO 9564 - 1 / ANSI X9.8 Format 0 ' 04 ' : Plus format ' 05 ' : ISO 9564 - 1 / ANSI X9.8 Format 1 ' 47 ' : ISO 9564 - 1 / ANSI X9.8 Format 3 '48': ISO 9564 - 1 / ANSI X9.8 Format 4 Primary Account Number (PAN) The Primary Account Number, used to form the PIN Block. n N If ' PIN Block Format Code ' = ' 48 ' : The 12 - 19 digit PAN, in cluding the check digit. If present, the delimiter below must also be present. or 18 H If ' PIN Block Format Code ' = ' 04 ' : The 18 digit PAN excluding the check digit. If the PAN is less than 18 digits, it must be right - justified and padded with ' F ' s on the left. or 12 N For all other values of ' PIN Block Format Code ' : The 12 right - most digits of the PAN, excluding the check digit."
