    "source": "Thales payShield 10K Host Command Reference v1.9, Section 2.1, Command P4 (p. 682)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command P4 (P5) - Generate a Proof of Host value\n\n- **Command Code:** `P4`\n- **Response Code(s):** `P5`\n- **Manual Page:** 682\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTo generate a value for the host to send to the PIN pad to prove the host is the bona fide host for the terminal. As per AS2805 6.4 terminal key management.\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `P4` |\n| Terminal Master Key 1 | 1 A | + 32 H or |\n| 1 A + | 48 H |  TMK1, encrypted under Variant 1 of LMK pair 14 - 15 |\n| PPASN (LMK) | 16 H | PPASN, encrypted under Variant 8 of LMK pair 14 - 15 |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Must be present if a message trailer is present. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Optional. Maximum length 32 characters . |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `P5` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n| Host Proof | 8 H | The value for host proof of endpoint |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Present only if present in the command message. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command P4 (P5) - Generate a Proof of Host value\n\n- **Command Code:** `P4`\n- **Response Code(s):** `P5`\n- **Manual Page:** 682\n- **Firmware Version:** payShield 10K v1.9\n\n---\n\n### Function\n\nTo generate a value for the host to send to the PIN pad to prove the host is the bona fide host for the terminal. As per AS2805 6.4 terminal key management.\n\n### Command Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Command Code | 2 A | Value `P4` |\n| Terminal Master Key 1 | 1 A | + 32 H or |\n| 1 A + | 48 H |  TMK1, encrypted under Variant 1 of LMK pair 14 - 15 |\n| PPASN (LMK) | 16 H | PPASN, encrypted under Variant 8 of LMK pair 14 - 15 |\n| Delimiter | 1 A | Value ' % ' . Optional; if present, the following field must also be present . |\n| LMK Identifier | 2 N | LMK identifier; min value = ' 00 ' ; max value is defined by license; must be present if the above Delimiter is present. |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Must be present if a message trailer is present. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Optional. Maximum length 32 characters . |\n\n### Response Message\n\n| Field | Length & Type | Details |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| Message Header | m A | Returned to Host unchanged |\n| Response Code | 2 A | Value `P5` |\n| Error Code | 2 A | `'00'` : No error, or standard two-digit error code |\n| Host Proof | 8 H | The value for host proof of endpoint |\n| End Message Delimiter | 1 C | Present only if present in the command message. Value X ' 19. |\n| Message Trailer | n A | Present only if present in the command message. Maximum length 32 characters. |\n\n"
    }
